{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 1"},"body":"The captured configured assertion and the cited paper assertion were read with their relevant definitions; the disclosed relation follows the stated scope, not the previous frontend choice.\n\nInspected: Read paperMain and the symmetric integer Fourier-sum convention on AddCircle (2π).","content_sha256":"sha256:037cd64e4daaf1c2a8a81e2828474b24409698781d3d1168bcfa85368042eb6d","fingerprint":"sha256:2d86f625403e31c67ed8b7c54fa697466a2e1f303401bfca9de00596f33eee4f","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. The captured configured assertion and the cited paper assertion were read with their relevant definitions; the disclosed relation follows the stated scope, not the previous frontend choice.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:c4d23b5ee24bd446a0524df1e3af08c7ea7d293e079cc8c8d6030113bdb5ab3f","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.FourierLLogL.paperMain"],"explanation":"The Lean assertion assumes almost-everywhere strong measurability and integrability of ‖f‖ log(2+‖f‖) on the circle. It concludes convergence of the symmetric Fourier partial sums to f away from a measurable null set, matching the paper’s almost-everywhere L log L assertion.","fingerprint":"sha256:9bc621d15616d701e6f4afc2678ba68673fa5d03f53a0e93ac615db4c82a785a","limitations":"Source-level formulation comparison only; this is not independent verification of the definitions, Lean proof, or manuscript proof.","relation":"same-claim","row_id":"Almost-everywhere-Fourier-convergence-in-L-log-L-September-23-2026#thm:main","statement_sha256":"sha256:e2a2e6ba1cd